TYPES.md §12.1, §3.6: a method written in a variant body outside any case is a member of every case, so naming it `kind` is E2105, as in a case body.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local variant Reward {
  item { count: Int }
  nothing

  fn kind(self) -> Int { return 1 }
}
-- findings.txt --
error[E2105]  a/a.canon:7:6
  kind is reserved on variant cases

